@* A section RCL does NOT inherit the host's Views/_ViewImports.cshtml. Omitting a line
   here ships broken markup with a green build and no runtime error — see design §1/§2.

   Three localizers by design (design §15 step 3b, Governance's two-marker variant plus
   one): the section owns its 67 Onboarding_* / OnboardingReview_* / OnboardingBanner_*
   keys; SharedResource keeps the genuinely shared vocabulary the widget renders
   (Common_*, Shifts_*) and the three Onboarding_*Label keys MVC's global
   DataAnnotationLocalizerProvider resolves; and the widget's Consents step renders
   Consent's copy through Consent's own _ConsentReviewBody partial.

   The review pages' three <vc:> elements resolve as follows: <vc:human> is already in
   Humans.UI, while <vc:profile-card> and <vc:access-matrix> read Shell-owned registries
   and stay there — both are invoked by name instead (design §15 step 6, CityPlanning's
   and Governance's cases). Guarded by OnboardingPageRenderTests (step 12). *@
@using Humans.Application.DTOs
@using Humans.Application.Extensions
@using Humans.Consent
@using Humans.Consent.Contracts
@using Humans.Domain.Enums
@using Humans.Onboarding
@using Humans.Onboarding.Controllers
@using Humans.Onboarding.Models
@using Humans.UI
@using Humans.UI.Extensions
@using Humans.UI.Models
@using Humans.UI.Models.Tables
@using Humans.UI.ViewComponents
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Localization
@inject IStringLocalizer<OnboardingResource> Localizer
@inject IStringLocalizer<SharedResource> SharedLocalizer
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
@addTagHelper *, Humans.UI
